<title>UK: Denmark sets $210 million bond due August 2000.</title>
<headline>Denmark sets $210 million bond due August 2000.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced</p>
<p>by joint lead managers IBJ International and New Japan</p>
<p>Securities Europe Ltd.</p>
<p> BORROWER   DENMARK, KINGDOM OF</p>
<p> AMT    $210 MLN	COUPON     5.72	MATURITY    18.AUG.00</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  PAR	 PAY DATE    18.FEB.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.20	LISTING    NONE	PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  AA1	 DENOMS (K) 10	  SALE LIMITS US/UK/JP</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.20	SELL CONC  1.0	 PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
